[ti:Day 13]

[00:00.00]controversial 例 In recent years, economic growth has become a controversial goal. 近几年，经济增长 成了一个有争议的目标。
[00:11.08]grievance 例 The personnel manager promised he would look into the grievances of the office staff. 人 事经理承诺将调查职员对公司的不满。
[00:24.06]assess 例 He was invited to assess the local purchasing power. 他被邀请去评估当地的购买 力。
[00:32.13]extra-territoriality 例 Generally speaking, the diplomat enjoys extra-territoriality. 一般说来，外交官享有治外 法权。
[00:44.33]offset 例 The extra cost of travelling is offset by the lower price of houses here. 旅游的额外花费被 这里较低的房租弥补回来了。
[00:54.93]pay 例 He doesn't like the job, but the pay is good. 他不喜欢那份工作，但那份工作薪水很高。
[01:01.27]covenant 例 The covenant of the League of Nations bound all signatory states not to go to war. 国 际联盟盟约规定，所有签字国都不得诉诸战争。
[01:13.30]foul 例 You might fall foul of the law by parking your car here. 你把车停在这里可能是违法的。
[01:21.22]exposure 例 Investing too much money into the same industry could lead to a big credit exposure. 往同一个行业投入太多的钱会导致很大的信贷风 险。
[01:33.72]salutation 例 The singer bowed deeply as a salutation of thanks. 那位歌手深深鞠躬表示感谢。
[01:42.11]graph 例 Our marketing review has been displayed in the form of a graph. 我们已经用图表的形式展示 了营销报告。
[01:51.30]opening 例 The company has about 10 job openings for English editors and educational software designers. 那家公司有10个左右关于英文编辑和 教育软件设计者的岗位空缺。
[02:05.23]fold 例 Many start-ups folded during the economic downturn. 很多新兴公司在经济低迷时期都倒闭 了。
[02:13.15]adjust 例 The central bank recently adjusted its interest rate to keep commodity prices stable. 为了保持物价稳定，中央银行近期对利率进行了 调整。
[02:25.81]onus 例 Sine the accident, they have been trying to shift the onus for passenger safety onto the local government. 事故发生后，他们一直试图将 负责乘客安全的责任推给当地政府。
[02:40.69]grimy 例 He could see grimy roofs, factory chimneys and church spires at the crossroads. 站在路 口，他可以看到肮脏的屋顶、工厂的烟囱和教堂 的尖顶。
[02:52.25]inconceivable 例 It is inconceivable that he could be considered for the position. 他被当做这个职位 的人选真是令人难以置信。
[03:03.18]enormous 例 Enormous expenses are needed to afford a luxury life. 奢侈的生活是由巨额开销支撑的。
[03:11.72]backlog 例 Our on-line store had an order backlog of 2 million dollars last month. 上个月，我们的网 上商店积压了200万美元的订单。
[03:22.33]empower 例 The normal user is only empowered for the file reading authorisation. 一般用户只有阅读文 档的权限。
[03:32.94]over-demand 例 The measures alleviated the difficulties such as over-demand in the electronics market. 这些措施缓解了电子市场面临的需求过量 的问题。
[03:46.87]pinpoint 例 We are still unable to pinpoint the cause of the industrial accident. 我们依然不能确定这次 工伤事故的原因。
[03:57.48]sag 例 The dollar held up well today but the pound sagged. 今日，美元依旧坚挺，但英镑下跌。
[04:04.76]smudge 例 Be careful and don't smudge the photo. 小 心点，别把照片弄脏。
[04:10.94]jurisdiction 例 The British police have no jurisdiction over foreign bank accounts. 外国银行账户不在英国 警方的管辖权限之内。
[04:22.18]grope 例 I am groping for the light switch in the dark room. 我在一片漆黑的屋里摸索着寻找电灯开 关。
[04:29.62]fatal 例 The short-sighted policy led to fatal results. 这个目光短浅的政策导致了致命的后果。
[04:36.90]market-led 例 The products of the company are market- led. 这家公司的产品做到了以市场为导向。
[04:44.50]headhunt 例 Our company encourages its staf f to headhunt as a sideline for recruiting qualified personnel. 我们公司鼓励员工兼职猎头，为公司 物色合格的人才。
[04:58.75]antitrust 例 Some of the biggest antitrust cases were initiated by complaints taken to the Justice Department. 一些规模很大的反垄断案例都是由 向司法部提起申诉开始的。
[05:13.48]adjoin 例 It is allowed to adjoin to the packages of merchandise some promotional advertisements. 在商品包装盒上附贴一些促销广 告是可以的。
[05:26.46]peril 例 Remember that you do it at your own peril. 记住，你这样做是要自担风险的。
[05:32.79]function 例 His post should be determined only by his function in the company. 他的职位应该视其在 公司所起的作用而定。
[05:42.92]episode 例 It is an episode that he never wishes to ment ion. 那是一段他永远不愿提及的经历。
[05:50.52]finance 例 The finance budget has been hacked almost in half. 财政预算几乎被削减了一半。
[05:58.44]wobble 例 Our company's shares wobbled with the news of a takeover bid. 征购消息一传出，我们 公司的股票就出现了波动。
[06:07.62]cram 例 System vendors continue to cram more functions into their kernels. 系统供应商继续将 更多的功能塞进核心程序。
[06:17.44]credit 例 China's great economic moderation has necessarily been accompanied by sharply rising credit. 中国经济的大幅度调整必然伴随着 信贷的急剧增长。
[06:31.37]conversion 例 There are no charges for currency conversion or handling. 货币兑换或处理不会收 取费用。
[06:40.87]deed 例 The law has detailed rules on applications for notarisation, the verification process and the issuance of the notary deed. 该法律对公证 申请、认证程序和公证人证书的颁发都作了详细 的规定。
[06:58.13]shed 例 The company had to shed those who'd been there for a short time due to the economic crisis. 由于经济危机，公司不得不将 临时工解雇。
[07:10.64]engineer 例 He's engineered several big industrial projects. 他已监造过几个大型工业项目。
[07:18.87]bolster 例 The new government will take necessary measures to bolster economic growth. 新政府 将采取必要措施来促进经济增长。
[07:30.43]deviate 例 The recent weather deviates from the norm for this time of year. 最近的天气与往年这时候 的天气不一样。
[07:40.08]mandate 例 The company mandated him to deal with the business case. 公司委托他来处理这个商业 案例。
[07:48.79]engage 例 Human Resources have engaged a new secretary for the manager. 人力资源部为经理新 聘了一位秘书。
[07:58.13]reciprocate 例 We are inclined to reciprocate in cooperation. 在这次合作中，我们倾向于互惠互 利。
[08:06.37]basis 例 On the basis of our research, we advised the firm to use new techniques for solving conflicts of interest within the team. 根据我们 的研究，我们建议公司采用新技术来解决团队内 部的利益冲突。
[08:23.31]kudos 例 She got a great deal of kudos for her excellent work in the company. 她因在公司的出 色工作而得到许多赞扬之声。
